{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4391382","formula":"C₂₃H₃₁N₃O","hill":"C23H31N3O","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":23.0,"H":31.0,"N":3.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"APINACA"},"descriptions":{"en":"APINACA (AKB48, N-(1-adamantyl)-1-pentyl-1H-indazole-3-carboxamide) is a drug that acts as a reasonably potent agonist for the cannabinoid receptors. It is a full agonist at CB1 with an EC50 of 142 nM and Ki of 3.24 nM (compared to the Ki of Δ9-THC at 28.35 nM and JWH-018 at 9.62 nM), while at CB2 it acts as a partial agonist with an EC50 of 141 nM and Ki of 1.68 nM (compared to the Ki of Δ9-THC at 37.82 nM and JWH-018 at 8.55 nM). Its pharmacological characterization has also been reported in a discontinued patent application."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":57404063,"mass":365.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCCCN1C2=CC=CC=C2C(=N1)C(=O)NC34CC5CC(C3)CC(C5)C4","inchikey":"UCTCCIPCJZKWEZ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"N-(1-adamantyl)-1-pentylindazole-3-carboxamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"57404063","atoms":58,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":8.437,"y":1.697,"z":0.179,"el":"C"},{"x":7.113,"y":0.95,"z":0.234,"el":"C"},{"x":6.131,"y":1.478,"z":-0.812,"el":"C"},{"x":4.823,"y":0.684,"z":-0.87,"el":"C"},{"x":3.985,"y":0.811,"z":0.401,"el":"C"},{"x":2.705,"y":0.132,"z":0.273,"el":"N"},{"x":2.441,"y":-1.186,"z":0.547,"el":"C"},{"x":3.25,"y":-2.235,"z":1.007,"el":"C"},{"x":2.657,"y":-3.492,"z":1.158,"el":"C"},{"x":1.313,"y":-3.693,"z":0.852,"el":"C"},{"x":0.519,"y":-2.636,"z":0.392,"el":"C"},{"x":1.09,"y":-1.354,"z":0.248,"el":"C"},{"x":0.635,"y":-0.064,"z":-0.176,"el":"C"},{"x":1.641,"y":0.83,"z":-0.157,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.726,"y":0.33,"z":-0.586,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.944,"y":1.142,"z":-1.48,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.732,"y":-0.274,"z":0.154,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.159,